prompt:
Generate 60 realistic ONE-OFF requests a developer might type to Claude Code (an AI coding agent) while working in a ios-app project, roughly in the area of: documentation (READMEs, API docs generation, ADRs, docstrings, doc sites). Batch 6: vary them widely and make each a distinct, specific task that would not be repeated (a particular bug, a specific refactor, a question about one file, a single investigation). Mix lengths and styles (casual, terse, detailed). Include some that are only questions/explanations.

For each, give the tool calls Claude would make (1-6 steps) using ONLY these shapes:
  {"tool": "Bash", "command": "<shell command>"}
  {"tool": "Edit" | "Write" | "Read", "file": "<repo-relative path>"}
  {"tool": "Grep", "pattern": "<regex>", "path": "<dir>"}
  {"tool": "mcp", "server": "<linear|jira|github|slack|notion|sentry>", "name": "<tool_name>", "args": ["<arg names>"]}
  {"tool": "WebFetch", "url": "<url>"}
Questions may have only Read/Grep steps.

Reply with ONLY JSON: {"items": [{"prompt": "...", "trace": [...]}, ...]}

